h the MT evaluation setting\n2299\tof xCOMET-XL (i.e., src + ref) by using the full\n2300\tsource language article as the source text, the reference summary and the predicted summary (Guerreiro et al., 2024). As shown in Table 4, the resulting model rankings are consistent across both the\n2301\tMT and QE configurations.\n2302\tROUGE-L Given that BERTScore and\n2303\txCOMET exhibit the highest correlation with\n2304\thuman judgment, we have prioritized these two\n2305\tmetrics as our primary evaluation measures.\n2306\t\n2307\t\fLanguage\n2308\t\n2309\tX-Comet-XL\n2310\t\n2311\tBERTScore F1 (ref)\n2312\t\n2313\tTrans→Sum\n2314\t\n2315\tSum→Trans\n2316\t\n2317\tTrans.→Sum.\n2318\t\n2319\tSum→Trans\n2320\t\n2321\tAmharic\n2322\tArabic\n2323\tBengali\n2324\tChinese\n2325\tFrench\n2326\tGujarati\n2327\tHindi\n2328\tIndonesian\n2329\tJapanese\n2330\tKorean\n2331\tKyrgyz\n2332\tPersian\n2333\tPortuguese\n2334\tPunjabi\n2335\tRussian\n2336\tSinhala\n2337\tSpanish\n2338\tSwahili\n2339\tTamil\n2340\tTelugu\n2341\tThai\n2342\tTurkish\n2343\tUkrainian\n2344\tVietnamese\n2345\t\n2346\t0.246\n2347\t0.272\n2348\t0.214\n2349\t0.328\n2350\t0.246\n2351\t0.237\n2352\t0.234\n2353\t0.273\n2354\t0.288\n2355\t0.258\n2356\t0.252\n2357\t0.283\n2358\t0.290\n2359\t0.227\n2360\t0.339\n2361\t0.218\n2362\t0.259\n2363\t0.221\n2364\t0.201\n2365\t0.232\n2366\t0.327\n2367\t0.279\n2368\t0.319\n2369\t0.278\n2370\t\n2371\t0.228\n2372\t0.241\n2373\t0.205\n2374\t0.322\n2375\t0.223\n2376\t0.212\n2377\t0.215\n2378\t0.270\n2379\t0.276\n2380\t0.233\n2381\t0.224\n2382\t0.270\n2383\t0.274\n2384\t0.204\n2385\t0.300\n2386\t0.206\n2387\t0.254\n2388\t0.219\n2389\t0.196\n2390\t0.208\n2391\t0.311\n2392\t0.242\n2393\t0.284\n2394\t0.249\n2395\t\n2396\t0.711\n2397\t0.756\n2398\t0.666\n2399\t0.774\n2400\t0.708\n2401\t0.646\n2402\t0.652\n2403\t0.674\n2404\t0.731\n2405\t0.677\n2406\t0.706\n2407\t0.682\n2408\t0.657\n2409\t0.648\n2410\t0.701\n2411\t0.702\n2412\t0.682\n2413\t0.665\n2414\t0.675\n2415\t0.668\n2416\t0.619\n241